{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q1090011","formula":"Li₂NH","hill":"HLi2N","elements":["H","Li","N"],"composition":{"H":1.0,"N":1.0,"Li":2.0},"names":{"en":"Lithium imide","ru":"Имид лития","uk":"Імід літію"},"descriptions":{"en":"Lithium imide is an inorganic compound with the chemical formula Li2NH. This white solid can be formed by a reaction between lithium amide and lithium hydride. LiNH2 + LiH → Li2NH + H2 The product is light-sensitive and can undergo disproportionation to lithium amide and characteristically red lithium nitride. 2 Li2NH → LiNH2 + Li3N Lithium imide is thought to have a simple face-centered cubic structure with a Fm3m space group; with N-H bond distances of 0.82(6) Å and a H–N–H bond angle of 109.5°, giving it a similar structure to lithium amide.","ru":"Имид лития — неорганическое вещество с формулой Li2NH, может рассматриваться как производное аммиака. Белый порошок, реагирует с водой.","uk":"Імі́д лі́тію — неорганічна сполука складу Li2NH, може розглядатися як похідна аміаку. Безбарвні кристали, що реагують з водою."},"fame":11,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-699284","atoms":78,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[7.1,0.0,0.0],[0.0,7.13,0.0],[0.0,0.0,10.089]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":0.0,"y":1.782,"z":6.227,"el":"Li"},{"x":7.1,"y":1.782,"z":6.227,"el":"Li"},{"x":0.0,"y":5.347,"z":3.862,"el":"Li"},{"x":7.1,"y":5.347,"z":3.862,"el":"Li"},{"x":3.55,"y":5.347,"z":6.291,"el":"Li"},{"x":3.55,"y":1.782,"z":3.798,"el":"Li"},{"x":3.55,"y":5.347,"z":3.976,"el":"Li"},{"x":3.55,"y":1.782,"z":6.113,"el":"Li"},{"x":1.775,"y":5.347,"z":2.522,"el":"Li"},{"x":5.325,"y":5.347,"z":2.522,"el":"Li"},{"x":5.444,"y":3.619,"z":8.923,"el":"Li"},{"x":5.444,"y":3.511,"z":1.166,"